WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.870
You were able to picture it, I see.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.280
Yes, this is Vanguard!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.490
But, this is fun, Kai!

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:24.560
Just as I thought. You are Aichi Sendou.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.600
That's right, Kai.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.750
And this is the power that 
you gave me back then.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.750
I see.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.230
Stand up, my avatar!

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.170
Ride!

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.740
Blaster Blade!

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.050
Blaster Blade?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.510
So he rides Blaster Blade now? 
Man, what luck the guy's got.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.980
I activate Blaster Blade's ability.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.960
Paying a cost of 2, I retire one 
of my opponent's rear-guards.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.740
Ride to Victory

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.420
I remember, Aichi Sendou.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.860
You were all beat-up back then.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:12.430
Yes. Back then I was always getting beaten 
up. It was hard for me to even go to school.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.550
It was like I was being suffocated 
by the small world around me...

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.280
Man, you're a mess.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.130
Lose a fight or somethin'?

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.560
Hey, wait up!

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.320
Here, take this.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.010
That's a pretty strong warrior there.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.920
What? Cheer up!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.400
Listen... Picture it in your mind.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.640
Picture yourself big and strong, 
like the warrior in that card!

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.880
I-I can't...

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.230
Well, sure, at first.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:07.210
But if you can picture it, one 
day you'll get that strength!

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.650
Get strong?

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.230
Your vision can become your power!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:22.630
Ever since I got that card, 
light has shone in my world.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.350
Since I got this Blaster Blade,

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.740
I've wanted to have a Vanguard fight with 
you, and obsessed over creating a deck.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.500
But soon afterwards, you moved away, Kai.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.870
Yes.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:41.380
But while I was making the deck, I forgot 
about all the bad and harsh things around me.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.640
I still can't picture myself any stronger,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:54.100
but the person who showed me the 
way to strength was you, Kai!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:59.400
I call the Knight of Silence, 
Gallatin, to the rear-guard!

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:05.870
That's why I'm so happy to have 
this Vanguard fight with you, Kai.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.180
I support Blaster Blade with 
Wingal, and attack Nehalem!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.210
He took damage!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.920
I support Marron with Flogal, 
and attack Nehalem once again!

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.890
Finally, I attack Nehalem with Gallatin!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.100
A triple attack?

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.150
Is this really the Aichi Sendou I know?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.840
5 damage...

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.220
One more and it's over.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.420
I guess Kai ain't such hot stuff after all!

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.500
But Kai over there isn't 
even breaking a sweat.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.500
He's gotta have some plan to win.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.000
It's your turn, Kai!

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.910
I showed you the way?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.330
You're taking me totally the wrong way.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:11.040
All I wanted to do was to 
get you hooked on Vanguard,

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.390
so I could collect rare cards from you later.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.540
Ooh, that's so evil!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.600
Was he gunning for me, too?

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.270
Kai, you wouldn't do things like that...

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.650
T-That's a lie! 
You're not that kind of person.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.530
Shut up!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.010
I am not the person you think I am!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:34.530
Don't go deciding who I am on your own!

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.330
I... I...

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.170
What was...

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.630
Just watch.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.800
This is who I really am!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.990
Ride the Vanguard!

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:53.820
Burn everything in this world to 
dust with your apocalyptic fire!

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.310
Dragonic Overlord!

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.030
W-Whoa...

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.160
That's the bastard that did me in!

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.380
This fight is over.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.090
I call two Monicas!

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:29.420
And at a cost of 3, I activate 
Dragonic Overlord's Counter Blast!

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:33.530
Dragonic Overlord's power increases by 5000!

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.270
Here I go.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.630
I support Bahr with Monica...

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.190
...and attack Blaster Blade!

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.980
I guard with Trumpeter!

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.040
Now it's their turn!

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:05.110
I support Monica with Jarran, 
and attack Blaster Blade!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.050
I guard with Gallatin!

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.100
He got through it!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.400
Used up your entire hand to defend, huh?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:36.410
But my attack isn't over yet!

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:40.160
Dragonic Overlord, it's your turn now!

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.760
With Aermo's support, attack Gallatin!

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:46.080
What? Gallatin?

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.080
And at the same time, 
check the drive trigger!

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.280
Gallatin is retired...

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.400
Dragonic Overlord... stands.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.060
What, didn't you know?

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:15.390
When Dargonic Overlord's skill, 
Counter Blast, is activated,

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:20.930
whenever it hits the opponent's rear-guard 
and defeats them, this unit stands!

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:25.620
It won't stop until everything 
in this world is burnt to dust!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:30.150
That's Dragonic Overlord's 
ability, Eternal Flame!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.350
Are you going to...

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:35.080
This time, attack Marron!

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.940
And at the same time, 
check the drive trigger!

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.240
M-Marron is also retired...

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:52.830
And once again, Dragonic Overlord stands!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.000
Oh, no...

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.050
No goin' easy on him, eh?

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:00.630
Damn it, I want one of those cards!

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:04.070
If I had me one, it'd be straight 
wins for me, no question about it!

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.640
Now, it's time for the main show.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.690
I attack Blaster Blade 
with Dragonic Overlord!

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:16.730
Check the trigger...

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.180
Get!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.360
Activate drive trigger!

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:25.500
Tahr's effect adds 5000 to 
Dragonic Overlord's attack power!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:36.880
And the effect of the critical 
trigger adds +1 to the damage!

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.150
That means...

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.990
That's 2 damage in addition 
to the 4 you already have.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.000
It's over.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.660
Yup, it's over.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.010
That's one...

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.640
And two...

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.090
This is...

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.680
Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine, eh?

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:12.920
What's this?

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.250
Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.230
A heal trigger.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.730
When that card appears,

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:25.830
you can recover a card from your damage zone 
as long as you have more than your opponent.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.010
In that case...

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:29.000
The fight isn't over yet.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:32.630
Now I have 5 cards in my damage zone.

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:39.580
It's your turn, Aichi Sendou.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.390
Kai...

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.450
Now it's Aichi's attack.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.740
Kai's got 5 damage.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.870
If he can just damage Kai 
once, then the fight's over.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.410
So Aichi's actually gonna win?

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:56.090
No telling yet!

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:59.530
It's plenty possible that Kai hangs tough.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:04.800
I don't believe what you said before.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:05.570
What?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:11.670
You said that you gave me Blaster Blade 
so that you could collect my cards.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.580
But if that's the case,

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:20.610
then this Blaster Blade wouldn't have 
given me the courage that it did!

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:23.160
Ridiculous...

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:30.600
No... No matter what you try and say, 
Blaster Blade has been really important to me!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.730
And that's never going to change!

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:39.110
I can picture how I was when I took 
that Blaster Blade from you...

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.610
And how you were back then, too!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.610
The picture in my mind is the truth!

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.400
I can picture this fight...

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:53.540
I can picture my Blaster 
Blade defeating you, Kai!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.830
I call Elaine!

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.070
I support Elaine with Flogal...

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.600
....and attack Dragonic Overlord!

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.240
I guard with Tahr!

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.820
Your attack does not go through.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.950
He defended, just like we thought!

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.140
What's gonna happen?

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:30.270
If he can defend, then next turn it 
will be impossible to defend completely

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:31.530
against Kai's triple attack.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.080
In other words, Kai will win.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.740
There is only one more attack.

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:39.790
And he has one defensive card in his hand.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:41.390
However...

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.180
He has a defense power of 21000.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:54.080
The attack power of Blaster Blade is 9000, 
plus Wingal's 6000, and the ability adds 4000...

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:55.930
It won't be enough.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.730
This will be the end!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.710
Attack, Blaster Blade!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.260
This will be the end!

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.280
Attack, Blaster Blade!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:36.090
Kai, it's always been my dream 
to fight with you like this!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.560
Attack, Blaster Blade!

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:48.710
I guard with Tahr!

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:55.860
With this, your attack will not go through.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:58.900
It's not going to be enough...

00:14:58.900 --> 00:14:59.770
Please!

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.860
Check for a drive trigger!

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:10.930
This is...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.020
Drive trigger activated.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:17.760
Attack power +5000, damage +1.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.310
Which means...

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:49.920
Dragonic Overlord was defeated 
from Blaster Blade's hit.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.930
I have now returned to merely a spirit.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.500
And I have been extinguished 
off the planet Cray...

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:57.680
Kai...

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:01.630
I... have lost.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.690
You beat Kai!

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:16.520
Kai!

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.730
Yeah, that card is yours after all.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.430
Kai...

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.000
Kai, hey!

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:30.530
Hey!

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:31.430
Kai!

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:36.220
Thank you!

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:39.720
Hey, Kai!

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:42.830
Thank you...

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.240
I think we should head home...

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.490
Hey, you forgot your bag!

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.400
Oh, crap...

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.380
When I saw you under the apple tree...

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.600
With your hair swept up for the first time...

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.080
Who is the poet that wrote this?

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.910
Aichi Sendou!

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:20.980
R-Right!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.020
Um... Um...

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:24.990
It might be a French person!

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.880
Is it Peynet?

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.170
Takuboku Ishikawa, duh!

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:31.360
No, no... It's Wakako Shimazaki!

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.720
He doesn't know!

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.400
You guys are too much, really!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.480
Um... Touson?

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.300
Blaster... Blade.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:54.390
Let's go!

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.780
Heading to Card Capital today again?

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.340
Well, of course!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.220
Check out my deck!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.350
You sure like it...

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:03.880
Oh, you got it backwards.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:06.310
Vanguard likes <i>me</i>!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.710
Morikawa!

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:09.680
What do you want?

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:13.950
I was hoping I could have a Vanguard 
fight with you next time...

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.070
You wanna beat me?

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:18.260
No...

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:25.370
I just don't know much about Vanguard yet, 
so I was hoping you would teach me...

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:31.500
Teach you? A small fry like 
you ain't worth my time.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.520
Y-Yeah...

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.540
Small fry, huh?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:38.200
Man, Kai's so lame!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:43.200
He acts like he's all that and then goes 
and loses to a small fry like Aichi!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.400
Yeah, totally!

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.030
If I were him I'd never show 
my face in the store again!

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.100
Hey, let's have a cardfight!

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.550
Yeah, let's!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.480
I made a new deck.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.830
You think it can beat my ultimate deck?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:13.400
Oh yeah? Well, mine is the 
ultimate times infinity!

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:17.020
Well, then mine's the 
ultimate, super ultimate...

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:20.010
Then mine's the super duper ultimate...

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:23.050
Picture yourself big and strong!

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:27.720
That's right...

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:32.270
I'm a Royal Paladin, the strongest knight...

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:35.470
I'm going to get stronger, and stronger!

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:42.140
Kai...

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.000
Hello.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.050
Welcome.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.460
No one is here.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.390
That's because it's still early.

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:20.370
I see.

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.610
Yeah, that's true.

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.500
Are you waiting for someone?

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:45.370
Yes, but I'm not sure he's coming.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.830
Since I won, he might not be coming back.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:54.080
And I after I finally met Kai again...

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.170
Oh, I doubt that.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.660
Kai!

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.890
Hey, Aichi. What're you doing here?

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:16.460
Hey, guy from yesterday!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.210
Um, you see...

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.900
Say no more!

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.830
How about I play you today?

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:28.850
No, I think I'll be the 
one playing him today!

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.010
Me, too!

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:33.920
What?

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:37.310
Morikawa, and Izaki, too!

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.200
That was rich!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.740
Why are you here?

00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:42.820
What a shock!

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:48.320
What are you guys so shocked about?

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.480
Did you seriously think we 
wouldn't show after that?

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:53.990
With hundreds of millions of people 
around the world playing card games,

00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:58.530
they've naturally become 
a part of our daily lives.

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:07.080
Cardfight! Vanguard is the card game 
that gets most of our attention now.

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:13.600
And one of those cards let 
me meet him once again.

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:54.850
Come on, Aichi! That whole thing about you 
being a beginner at Vanguard was a bluff, right?

00:23:54.850 --> 00:23:58.270
It's true! I'd never had 
a cardfight before...

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.250
It was my dream to be able 
to have one with Kai.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:03.930
Being satisfied after playing that 
guy? Yeah, that's the Aichi I know.

00:24:03.930 --> 00:24:06.210
Then will you play me next, Morikawa?

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:10.640
I'll show you all my awesome skills!

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:13.180
Next time: Welcome to Card Capital!

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:17.350
I'm picturing myself standing 
on the planet Cray...

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:19.040
...wait, Emi? Why are you here?
